Presidential elections were held in [[Republic of Serbia (1990–2006)|Serbia]] on 16 November 2003,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/1908/|title=Republic of Serbia: Election for Serbian Presidency|website=IFES Election Guide}}</ref> a month before the [[2003 Serbian parliamentary election|December 2003 parliamentary election]].<ref>[[Dieter Nohlen]] & Philip Stöver (2010) ''Elections in Europe: A data handbook'', p1715 {{ISBN|978-3-8329-5609-7}}</ref> Although [[Tomislav Nikolić]] of the [[Serbian Radical Party]] received the most votes, the elections were invalidated as voter turnout was just 39%, less than the 50% threshold required by electoral law. As a result, [[2004 Serbian presidential election|fresh elections]] were held in June 2004.

Two days after the election, the [[Democratic Opposition of Serbia]] coalition was dissolved.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 November 2003 |title=DOS prestao da postoji - 2003-11-18 |url=https://www.glasamerike.net/a/a-34-a-2003-11-18-13-1-87061457/762195.html |access-date=30 December 2023 |website=Glas Amerike |language=sr}}</ref>

